{"title":"16","section":"1220c","heading":"Denial of applications; finality of decision","lead":"A decision by the Secretary denying any application for a 1 obsolete ship under this chapter is final.","tree":[],"notes":[{"topic":"amendments","heading":"Amendments","text":"1984—Pub. L. 98–623 substituted “obsolete ship” for “Liberty ship”."}],"sourceCredit":"(Pub. L. 92–402, § 6, Aug. 22, 1972, 86 Stat. 618; Pub. L. 98–623, title II, § 207(1), Nov. 8, 1984, 98 Stat. 3397.)","releasePoint":"119-102","ancestors":[{"type":"title","num":"Title 16—","heading":"CONSERVATION","identifier":"/us/usc/t16"},{"type":"chapter","num":"CHAPTER 25B—","heading":"REEFS FOR MARINE LIFE CONSERVATION","identifier":"/us/usc/t16/ch25B"}]}